{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And we have heard, and we will do.</b> It says <b>and we have heard</b> because they said to Moses that he should reply to HaShem regarding the statement ״בַּעֲבוּר יִשְׁמַע הָעָם בְּדַבְּרִי עִמָּךְ״ (Exodus 19:9) — that their desire was to hear from the mouth of HaShem and not from the mouth of a disciple. Therefore now they went back and said something seemingly contradictory to their earlier words: ״וְשָׁמַעְנוּ״ etc. And it says <b>and we will do</b> — the Jews upheld and accepted to do all His words as though they had heard from the mouth of the Shekhinah."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:15:26.505152433Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}